> Separate recognition from generation

The lower hidden bias belongs to recognition only. Replacing it with100 changes inferred recognition probabilities but leaves the exact generative likelihood unchanged. The two printed NLL values must agree exactly.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/deep_belief_worked.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){namespace n=dm::nn;namespace m=n::models;std::filesystem::create_directories("build");n::ParameterStore p(21003),q(21003);m::RbmParameters(p,8,4);m::RbmParameters(q,4,3);auto x=m::BinaryStates(8);auto before=m::DeepBelief(p,q,x);p.set("hidden_bias",n::full({4},100));auto after=m::DeepBelief(p,q,x);auto values=n::stack({before.nll,after.nll,n::sum(n::exp(after.log_probability))},0);if(before.nll.item()!=after.nll.item())return 1;
std::print("| coordinate | computed value |\n|---:|---:|\n");auto v=values.to_vector<double>();for(size_t i=0;i<v.size();++i)std::print("| {} | {:.9f} |\n",i,v[i]);n::save_npz("build/deep_belief_worked.npz",{{"values",values}});dm::graphics::RPlot::create().bars(n::arange(0,std::int64_t(v.size())).to_vector<double>(),v,"native values",{37,99,235}).title("Separate recognition from generation").size(1000,550).save_svg("build/deep_belief_worked.svg");}
```
